    "title": "Severe Thunderstorm Warning by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 hours ago Check NWS updates here\nEffective: 2025-09-10 21:16:00 MDT Expires: 2025-09-10 22:15:00 MDT Urgency: Immediate Severity: Severe Certainty: Observed Instruction: For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a building. Target Area: Custer, SD; Lawrence, SD; Pennington, SD; Weston, WY SVRUNR\nThe National Weather Service in Rapid City has issued a\n* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for... Northwestern Custer County in southwestern South Dakota... Southwestern Lawrence County in west central South Dakota... West central Pennington County in west central South Dakota... East central Weston County in northeastern Wyoming...\n* Until 1015 PM MDT.\n* At 915 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located 4 miles southeast of Newcastle, moving northeast at 35 mph.\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and quarter size hail.\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\nIMPACT...Hail damage to vehicles is expected. Expect wind damage to roofs, siding, and trees.\n* Locations impacted include... Newcastle, Hill City, Silver City, Hisega, Rochford, Flag Mountain, Mystic, Moon, Four Corners, Deerfield, Deerfield Reservoir, Pactola Reservoir, O'Neil Pass, Medicine Mountain, Redbank Spring Campground, Sheridan Lake, Crooks Tower, Bear Mountain Lookout, Mallo Camp, and Black Fox Campground.",
